# lf002, the flood-watcher of the Heights (doc 84 §9.7): the luna table of rm_ada_aldwych, ported. Her husband by the
# slot, never by name.
mantle lf002
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light
tier standard
written_for rm_ada_aldwych
title the flood-watcher
fits stage=adult|old
traits temper=calm warmth=warm
quirk knows_which_streets_flood_first
likes dry_cellars
dislikes being_thought_soft
fears sudden_ruin
hopes a_quiet_old_age
topics weather +.4 home +.2
styles refuse=firm
marks saying
persona #self.first# keeps a careful house in the Heights: calm, warm to those who earn trust, and knows which streets flood first.

words
saying! = Pride doesn't keep a den dry | Patience is free; fairness isn't
pet!! = bright-tail | dear heart
greet[here.time=dawn|day] = Good day to you | Well met
greet = Well met | Evening

rule @home
when concept=bark working=no
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Take your time; there's no hurry. | The rain is finding the lower streets again.

scene floods
when concept=talk.weather
does tell.self / react.self
a : I know which streets flood first. The low ones always think it won't be them.
b[old] : Every spring the same.
b : And it always is.

line greet.return : #greet#, #pet#.
line farewell.return : #farewell#. Keep to the high side of the street.
line react.news.new : That's news. Truly.
line react.news.known : Yes. I'd heard it from the stairs.
line answer.how : Well, thank you. The cellar's dry, and that's a good week.
line tell.self [concept=talk.family self.married=yes self.spouse] : #self.spouse# worries about the drains more than I do, and that's saying something.
line reassure : It'll keep. Most things do, if you let them.

dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Come in from the rain.
